cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Calibrated for the Winter, Not for the Cold Snap: code and data for a chronological benchmark of 38 extreme-cold events in six U.S. power systems"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
authors:
  - family-names: Goehner
    given-names: Dresden
    email: dr.dresden0416@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-0366-7177"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Jurupa Valley, CA, USA"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DresdenGman/PJM-Cold-Calibration-Benchmark"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24010849
abstract: >-
  Code, plans, derived data and results for a chronological test of whether
  conformal 90% prediction intervals for day-ahead electricity load,
  calibrated on earlier winters, remain calibrated in the next extreme-cold
  event. 38 weather-defined events in PJM, MISO, ERCOT, SPP, NYISO and ISO-NE
  (2014-2026); two base forecasts (gradient-boosting quantile forecaster and
  the operators' EIA-930 day-ahead forecasts). Version 2.0.0 supersedes
  versions 1.0-1.2.
keywords:
  - probabilistic load forecasting
  - conformal prediction
  - extreme cold events
  - forecast evaluation
  - calibration
  - resource adequacy
